;; A thread's frames of slots (HE4d): an activation's slots come from its thread's arena, a stack of chunks, not
;; from Go's heap. Every frame of the thread's stack records the arena's top when it was pushed (Frame.mark); popping
;; it gives back everything above, the slots of the activations that ran since and have returned to it. The slots
;; never escape the stack: a closure, a constructor and a partial application copy their values out, only a case
;; frame keeps its activation's slots (below its own mark), and a continuation's capture (control0#) copies its
;; frames' slots to the heap first. A dead activation's slots below the top (a tail call to a larger frame) wait for
;; the next pop; past arenaMax a frame is Go's again.

